Hmmm... I recently played a submarine simulation game, where you get
some orders over the radio, you do it, report back, then you get new orders...
Do you really want to change nethack into this kind of military game? I love 
to do what I want to, in the order I choose... And after I got the Amulet
I'm so powerful, that I don't care any more what some old fool tries to tell
me to do ;-)

I like Peter's idea through - a question would be should we allow a player 
to keep the character and try another quest with it (once the first one is 
done)? That would probably be too easy - but people might like the idea...

>	Quibble: get some more powerful monsters... I don't know how
>you'd want to do this, but after the first couple levels of Ghennom, the
>rest is REAL boring, 'cause it's not really a challenge.  The only way
>of dying, really, is from a feature of the game you don't know about;
>for instance, my first character to get that far got fried by Moloch for
>praying.
>
That is how it should be. Don't make more powerful monsters. If we
really have to make late game more difficult - then by making mega-weapons
weaker, not by making monsters tougher. I think it should be possible to
win the game with no other atrifacts than the quest ones (i.e. your class
quest artifact plus the Amulet...). 

Actually I thing that currently the most difficult part of nethack is the 
'early middle game' - once you get to exp. level 7-10, but don't have enough 
decent equipment yet. If we were to wote about game balance adjustment - I'd
vote to readjust in this area first... Curently most my characters die 
around that time, and it seems to me that you need either an artifact
weapon or a really good armor, or a lot of luck to survive beyond that point.
